You're just missing the `Authorization` header. Add a Personal Access Token ([fine-grained](https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens) or [classic](https://github.com/settings/tokens)):

```json
"github": {
  "type": "remote",
  "url": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer ghp_your_token_here",
    "X-MCP-Toolsets": "repos,issues",
    "X-MCP-Readonly": "true"
  }
}
```

The HTTP 422 error is because GitHub doesn't support Dynamic Client Registration. Once PR #5940 is merged, you'll be able to use OAuth by configuring your own `clientId`/`clientSecret` - which is the recommended approach.
